package com.linguapro.android

object ScenarioBankB2 {
    private fun s(n: Int, text: String, a: ScenarioQuestion, b: ScenarioQuestion, transfer: String, c: ScenarioQuestion) =
        UnitScenario("B2-U$n", text, a, b, transfer, c)
    val items = listOf(
        s(1, "During a planning meeting, the sales team argued for an immediate launch, pointing to strong interest from customers. The support team was less confident because the training materials were incomplete. Instead of treating either concern as irrelevant, the chair proposed releasing the product to a small group first. Sales could test demand while support identified common questions. The proposal kept the launch moving, but made expansion conditional on the pilot's results rather than on enthusiasm alone.",
            sq("What does the compromise achieve?", "It tests demand while limiting an unprepared rollout.", "It guarantees that all customers will be satisfied.", "It permanently rejects the launch.", "Küçük grup, satışın talep testini ve desteğin hazırlığını birlikte mümkün kılar."),
            sq("What determines expansion?", "The pilot's results", "Enthusiasm alone", "The number of teams in the meeting", "Conditional on the pilot's results, genişlemenin ölçülen sonuca bağlı olduğunu belirtir."),
            "We support launching, provided that the pilot shows the support team can handle demand.",
            sq("What is the condition for support?", "Evidence of support capacity", "A launch without testing", "Cancelling customer contact", "Provided that, destek kapasitesi koşulunu koyar.")),
        s(2, "A report said that a new booking system reduced waiting times in two branches. It recommended wider use, but noted that both branches had unusually experienced staff. One manager described the findings as proof that the system would work everywhere. Another suggested testing it in a busier branch before expansion. The disagreement was not about whether the original results were positive; it was about how far those results could reasonably be generalised.",
            sq("What is the main disagreement?", "Whether the findings apply to other branches", "Whether the two branches used the system", "Whether waiting times were measured at all", "Generalised sonuçların farklı şubelere aktarılmasıyla ilgilidir."),
            sq("Which feature limits the evidence?", "The branches had unusually experienced staff.", "The system was never tested.", "All branches were included.", "Deneyimli personel, sonuçların her ortamı temsil etmesini sınırlar."),
            "The trial succeeded in a quiet branch, so the report recommends another test during peak demand.",
            sq("Why is another test useful?", "The original conditions may not represent peak demand.", "The first trial proved universal success.", "Quiet branches never use booking systems.", "Sakin ortamdan yoğun talebe genelleme ek kanıt ister.")),
        s(3, "An informal message asked a colleague to send the figures whenever she had a moment. Later, the same sender complained that the figures had not arrived before a board meeting. The colleague explained that the wording had suggested low urgency. A revised request kept a polite tone but stated a clear deadline and the reason for it. The lesson was not that politeness causes delays, but that vague politeness can conceal practical requirements.",
            sq("What caused the misunderstanding?", "Polite wording did not communicate urgency clearly.", "The colleague refused every request.", "The sender had stated a precise deadline.", "Whenever ... a moment düşük aciliyet izlenimi verir; açık son tarih yoktu."),
            sq("What did the revised message retain?", "Politeness alongside a clear deadline", "The original vagueness", "A claim that deadlines never matter", "Kibarlık korunurken deadline ve reason ekleniyor."),
            "Could you send the figures by noon? They are needed for today's board papers.",
            sq("Why is this request clearer?", "It combines politeness, timing and purpose.", "It avoids giving any deadline.", "It makes an unrelated personal complaint.", "By noon zamanı; board papers amacı; could you kibarlığı verir.")),
        s(4, "In a seminar, one student claimed that online courses were more effective because their completion rate was higher. Another pointed out that the online learners had chosen the format themselves and were older on average. The tutor asked the group to distinguish an observed difference from an explanation of that difference. They agreed that the figures were worth discussing, but did not by themselves establish that the teaching format caused the higher completion rate.",
            sq("What does the discussion distinguish?", "An observed association from a causal explanation", "A course title from a room number", "A completed trial from a cancelled seminar", "Farkın gözlenmesi ile formatın o farkı yaratması ayrı iddialardır."),
            sq("Which alternative explanation is mentioned?", "Differences between the learner groups", "A universal absence of teachers", "All learners using the same format", "Gönüllü seçim ve yaş farkı alternatif açıklamalardır."),
            "The users who chose the new system were already faster, so the comparison may not isolate its effect.",
            sq("What uncertainty remains?", "Whether the system caused the speed difference", "Whether any users existed", "Whether the old system had a name", "Already faster, başlangıç farkının etkiyi karıştırabileceğini gösterir.")),
        s(5, "A visitor declined dinner by saying that she had an early start the next day. Her host initially assumed that she disliked the invitation. A colleague suggested a more neutral interpretation: the visitor might simply need to rest. The host replied warmly and offered another occasion, without demanding a personal explanation. This preserved the relationship while recognising that an indirect refusal can communicate a practical limit rather than an unfriendly attitude.",
            sq("What interpretation does the colleague suggest?", "The refusal may reflect a practical need to rest.", "The visitor certainly dislikes the host.", "The invitation was never offered.", "Might simply need to rest, düşmanca niyetin kesin olmadığını gösterir."),
            sq("How does the host respond constructively?", "By offering another occasion without pressure", "By demanding proof of dislike", "By refusing all future contact", "Warmly ve another occasion, ilişkiyi baskı yaratmadan korur."),
            "I appreciate the invitation, but tomorrow starts very early for me. Perhaps another evening?",
            sq("What does the reply communicate?", "A polite refusal with an alternative", "A definite rejection of the relationship", "An acceptance for tonight", "Appreciate ve another evening, reddi kişisel kopuşa dönüştürmez.")),
        s(6, "A presentation displayed a large percentage increase in sales but omitted the original number of sales. When questioned, the presenter explained that the increase was from a small base. The audience still considered the growth encouraging, but wanted absolute figures and a longer comparison period before changing the budget. They were not rejecting percentages as useless; they were asking for enough context to judge the practical significance of the change.",
            sq("What did the audience need to interpret the percentage?", "The original numbers and a longer comparison", "A brighter slide colour", "A promise that all percentages are misleading", "Küçük başlangıç tabanı ve dönem, yüzde artışın ölçeğini anlamak için gereklidir."),
            sq("Was the growth dismissed entirely?", "No, it was encouraging but insufficiently contextualised.", "Yes, the audience denied any increase.", "No questions were asked.", "Encouraging olumlu değerlendirme; wanted absolute figures bilgi eksikliğidir."),
            "Sales doubled from two to four orders. The percentage is large, but the volume remains small.",
            sq("Which statement preserves the context?", "There was growth from a small base.", "There were millions of new orders.", "Sales fell by half.", "İki siparişten dörde çıkış, büyük yüzdeye rağmen küçük hacimdir.")),
        s(7, "Two departments blamed each other for delays. In a joint meeting, the facilitator asked each team to describe the handover rather than the other's personality. They discovered that one team thought an email confirmed readiness, while the other waited for a signed checklist. Agreeing on a shared handover signal reduced the immediate confusion. The discussion did not erase every disagreement, but turned a personal conflict into a process issue that could be addressed.",
            sq("What did the facilitator redirect attention towards?", "The handover process", "Personal insults", "An unrelated staffing competition", "Handover yerine kişilik yargılarından uzaklaşılması somut süreç sorununu görünür kılar."),
            sq("What mismatch caused confusion?", "Different signals for readiness", "A shared checklist everyone understood", "Both teams using identical assumptions", "Email ile signed checklist, hazır olma için farklı sinyallerdi."),
            "One team waits for approval; the other thinks sending the file is approval. They agree to use an explicit confirmation.",
            sq("What is the purpose of confirmation?", "Aligning different assumptions about approval", "Adding an unrelated competition", "Avoiding any communication", "Explicit confirmation ortak onay anlamını kurar.")),
        s(8, "A project leader was told to shorten the schedule without reducing the scope. The team explained that this would require either additional help or fewer checks. Rather than silently accepting all three demands, the leader listed the trade-offs and asked the sponsor to choose a priority. They agreed to preserve the safety checks and postpone a nonessential feature. The schedule became shorter because the scope changed, not because the constraints had somehow disappeared.",
            sq("How was the shorter schedule made feasible?", "A nonessential feature was postponed.", "All safety checks were removed.", "The original scope became effortless.", "Preserve safety checks ile postpone feature, kapsam değişikliği üzerinden çözüm kurar."),
            sq("What did the leader make explicit?", "The trade-offs between scope, time and resources", "That every demand could be met without cost", "That sponsors never set priorities", "Trade-offs, eşzamanlı taleplerin bedellerini görünür kılar."),
            "We can deliver earlier if we remove the optional dashboard, but the required checks will remain.",
            sq("What is conditional?", "Earlier delivery depends on reducing optional scope.", "Checks depend on hiding the change.", "The dashboard must be added first.", "If, erken teslimi isteğe bağlı kapsamın kaldırılmasına bağlar.")),
        s(9, "A researcher summarised three articles in an assignment. Initially, she listed them separately without explaining how their arguments related. Her supervisor asked her to group the findings around the research question and identify points of agreement and disagreement. In the revision, she distinguished what each source reported from her own interpretation. The result was a synthesis rather than a sequence of summaries, although the sources still had different methods and could not be treated as identical evidence.",
            sq("What improved in the revision?", "The sources were compared around a shared question.", "All source differences were erased.", "The research question was removed.", "Agreement/disagreement ve research question, kaynakları ilişkilendiren sentez yapısıdır."),
            sq("Which distinction was preserved?", "Source claims versus the writer's interpretation", "Article titles versus font colours only", "All sources as identical methods", "Each source reported ile own interpretation ayrılır."),
            "Two papers reach similar conclusions through different methods; the review notes both the agreement and the methodological difference.",
            sq("What makes this a balanced synthesis?", "It preserves agreement and relevant differences.", "It claims the methods are identical.", "It avoids discussing either conclusion.", "Sonuç benzerliği, yöntemlerin aynı olduğu anlamına gelmez.")),
        s(10, "Residents proposed reducing car access to a busy street. Shop owners worried about deliveries, while parents welcomed the possibility of safer crossings. The council invited both groups to design a trial with delivery hours and temporary barriers. It promised to review access problems as well as pedestrian use. The proposal therefore treated safety and business access as competing needs to accommodate, rather than assuming that either group had no legitimate concern.",
            sq("How does the trial address competing concerns?", "It combines delivery hours with temporary pedestrian measures.", "It permanently excludes every delivery.", "It ignores pedestrian safety.", "Delivery hours ve barriers, erişim ve güvenliği birlikte ele alır."),
            sq("What will the review consider?", "Both access problems and pedestrian use", "Only the number of council staff", "Only positive comments", "As well as, iki farklı değerlendirme alanını birlikte içerir."),
            "The trial will be reviewed for pedestrian safety and delivery access, not just popularity.",
            sq("Which evidence is relevant to the review?", "Effects on safety and practical access", "Only whether a slogan is memorable", "Only the colour of the barriers", "İki belirtilen ölçüt, değerlendirmeyi beğeniden daha kapsamlı kılar.")),
        s(11, "A speaker opened with a personal story, then moved to the problem the audience needed to solve. Her first draft contained several striking examples but no clear recommendation. After rehearsal, she removed an unrelated anecdote and stated the proposed action before giving supporting reasons. The revised talk still used a story to engage listeners, but the story now served the argument rather than replacing it. Questions at the end could therefore focus on the proposal's merits.",
            sq("What weakness did the first draft have?", "It lacked a clear recommendation.", "It contained no examples.", "It never used a personal story.", "No clear recommendation, ilgi çekici örneklerin eylem önerisine bağlanmadığını gösterir."),
            sq("What role does the story play in the revised talk?", "It supports the argument.", "It replaces all reasoning.", "It proves every claim automatically.", "Served the argument rather than replacing it, öykünün araç olarak konumunu açıklar."),
            "The anecdote draws attention, but the recommendation still needs evidence.",
            sq("What does this distinction prevent?", "Treating an engaging story as sufficient proof", "Using any example at all", "Stating a recommendation", "Dikkat çekme ve kanıtlama farklı işlevlerdir.")),
        s(12, "When a company introduced a new scheduling tool, managers sent instructions but did not ask how staff used the old system. Several employees kept private notes because the new tool lacked a familiar reminder. Some managers called this resistance to change. A workshop revealed that the notes addressed a genuine gap. Adding a reminder and explaining which records needed to be shared improved adoption more than repeating that the new system was compulsory.",
            sq("What did the workshop reveal?", "Some apparent resistance addressed a real practical gap.", "Every employee opposed all technology.", "The old system had never been used.", "Genuine gap, davranışın yalnızca değişim karşıtlığı olmadığını gösterir."),
            sq("What improved adoption?", "Adding a reminder and clarifying shared records", "Repeating compulsion without changes", "Removing all staff feedback", "Hatırlatıcı ve kayıt açıklığı, pratik ihtiyaca cevap verdi."),
            "Staff keep an extra list because the official system misses a necessary step.",
            sq("What should be examined before labelling this resistance?", "The unmet practical need", "Only the staff's willingness to obey", "The colour of the list", "Because ... misses a necessary step, karşılanmayan ihtiyacın neden olduğunu gösterir.")),
        s(13, "A project was reported as nearly complete because most individual tasks were finished. However, two unfinished tasks were necessary before any testing could begin. The manager revised the report to distinguish the amount of work completed from readiness for delivery. She assigned owners to the blocking tasks and scheduled a review before announcing a final date. This was less optimistic than the original report, but more useful for planning because it identified what still prevented progress.",
            sq("Why was 'nearly complete' potentially misleading?", "The remaining tasks blocked testing.", "No work had been done.", "Every task was equally unimportant.", "Az sayıda kalan iş, testin başlamasını engellediği için kritik önemdedir."),
            sq("What did the revised report distinguish?", "Completed work from delivery readiness", "Task names from employee birthdays", "Testing from all future work as irrelevant", "İşlerin bitme oranı ile teslim hazırlığı ayrı ölçütlerdir."),
            "Most tasks are finished, but integration has not begun and must precede delivery.",
            sq("Which conclusion is justified?", "Completion counts alone do not establish delivery readiness.", "Delivery has already happened.", "Integration is optional.", "Must precede delivery zorunlu ön koşuldur.")),
        s(14, "A brand claimed that its new packaging was environmentally friendly without explaining the comparison. Customers asked whether the claim referred to less material, easier recycling, or lower transport weight. The marketing team replaced the broad slogan with a specific statement about reduced packaging material and described what had not changed. The new wording was narrower, but it gave customers a claim they could understand and question rather than an attractive label with no clear basis.",
            sq("What improved in the revised claim?", "Its scope and basis became clearer.", "It covered every environmental impact conclusively.", "It removed all information about packaging.", "Specific statement ve what had not changed, iddianın sınırını açıklaştırır."),
            sq("Why was the original slogan questioned?", "It did not specify the relevant comparison.", "It contained detailed evidence for every impact.", "Customers had never seen packaging.", "Which comparison sorusu, geniş etiketin dayanağını arar."),
            "The box uses less cardboard; we make no claim about the product's total environmental impact.",
            sq("What does the statement deliberately limit?", "The claim to packaging material", "The customer's right to question it", "The meaning of cardboard to every material", "No claim about total impact, daha geniş çevresel sonuçların iddia edilmediğini belirtir.")),
        s(15, "A supplier offered a lower price if the customer committed to a longer contract. The customer valued flexibility because future demand was uncertain. Instead of arguing about the price alone, they discussed a shorter initial term with an option to extend. The supplier accepted a slightly higher initial price and a review date. Both sides gave up part of their first position while protecting the need that mattered most to them.",
            sq("What need mattered to the customer?", "Flexibility under uncertain demand", "The longest possible commitment regardless of need", "Avoiding any supply arrangement", "Future demand uncertain, uzun bağlanma yerine esneklik ihtiyacıdır."),
            sq("What was the compromise?", "A shorter term with an extension option", "The original longest contract at the lowest price", "No contract and no review", "Shorter initial term ve option to extend uzlaşmanın iki parçasıdır."),
            "We can accept the price if the initial commitment is shorter and renewal is optional.",
            sq("Which condition is requested?", "Limited initial commitment with a choice to renew", "Automatic lifelong renewal", "Immediate cancellation without supply", "If koşulu, süre sınırı ve isteğe bağlı yenilemedir.")),
        s(16, "An article linked a rise in household costs to several changes, including transport and energy prices. A commentator reduced the explanation to a single cause. The article itself was more cautious, noting that different households were affected differently. In class, students compared the simplified claim with the source and identified what had been left out. They did not need to agree on a policy response to recognise that the original explanation was broader than the commentator's version.",
            sq("What did the commentator simplify?", "A multi-cause explanation into one cause", "A single cause into many verified causes", "A price increase into a decrease", "Several changes kaynakta birden çok etken, single cause yorumda tek etken anlamına gelir."),
            sq("What could students recognise without agreeing on policy?", "That the source contained more nuance", "That one policy was conclusively best", "That all households were identical", "Kaynak ile sadeleştirme arasındaki fark, politika tercihinden bağımsız saptanabilir."),
            "The report names several factors, whereas the headline blames only one.",
            sq("What should an accurate summary avoid?", "Presenting the headline's single factor as the whole explanation", "Mentioning any factor", "Noting the report's complexity", "Several factors bilgisi korunmalıdır.")),
        s(17, "A prototype worked well in a laboratory demonstration. During a field trial, dust and irregular maintenance caused problems that the demonstration had not revealed. The development team treated this as useful information rather than as proof that the whole idea was worthless. They changed the casing and clarified maintenance requirements before another trial. Their report separated technical promise from readiness for ordinary use, allowing readers to see both progress and remaining limits.",
            sq("What did the field trial add?", "Information about conditions absent from the demonstration", "Proof that demonstrations never work", "A guarantee of immediate commercial readiness", "Dust ve irregular maintenance gerçek kullanım koşullarının farklılığını gösterir."),
            sq("How did the team interpret the problems?", "As evidence to guide improvements", "As a reason to hide all results", "As proof of universal failure", "Useful information ile tasarım ve bakım gereksinimleri iyileştirildi."),
            "The device succeeds under controlled conditions, but outdoor use remains untested.",
            sq("What is not yet established?", "Its performance outdoors", "Its performance in the controlled test", "Whether the device exists", "Remains untested, dış ortam başarısının henüz bilinmediğini belirtir.")),
        s(18, "Two organisations agreed on a service but used different meanings of urgent. One expected a reply within an hour; the other understood it as the next working day. Before signing, they replaced the vague term with specific response times and described exceptions for weekends. This did not remove every possible disagreement, but made a central expectation visible. A clause that sounds reassuring is not necessarily useful if the parties interpret its practical effect differently.",
            sq("What was clarified before signing?", "Response times and weekend exceptions", "Only the document's font", "A promise that all disputes are impossible", "Vague urgent yerine somut süreler ve istisnalar konuldu."),
            sq("Why was the original wording insufficient?", "The parties understood its effect differently.", "The word had no letters.", "Both parties already had identical expectations.", "Bir saat ile sonraki iş günü aynı hizmet beklentisi değildir."),
            "The agreement says 'promptly', but the parties disagree whether that means one hour or one day.",
            sq("Which revision would address the ambiguity?", "An explicit response-time definition", "Repeating 'promptly' in bold", "Removing every contact method", "Sorun yorum farkı olduğu için açık süre tanımı gerekir.")),
        s(19, "In a workshop, participants completed a task more slowly when the instructions changed halfway through. One observer described them as careless. Another noted that the new instructions conflicted with the first set. The facilitator asked what evidence would distinguish poor attention from an unclear procedure. The discussion shifted from judging people immediately to examining the conditions under which they worked. It remained possible that attention mattered, but the observed delay alone did not identify its cause.",
            sq("What alternative explanation was raised?", "Conflicting instructions", "An absence of participants", "A shorter task with no changes", "Yeni ve ilk yönergelerin çelişmesi gecikmeye alternatif açıklamadır."),
            sq("What does the delay alone establish?", "That performance slowed, not why it slowed", "That everyone was definitely careless", "That instructions had no effect", "Gözlem ile nedenin teşhisi ayrı tutulur."),
            "Errors rose after unclear instructions were introduced; this does not prove every participant ignored them.",
            sq("What distinction is preserved?", "A change in errors versus a claim about individual motives", "A claim that errors never occurred", "Proof of deliberate refusal by everyone", "Hata artışı, herkesin niyetini otomatik belirlemez.")),
        s(20, "The presenter began by listing every detail of a survey. The audience struggled to see why the figures mattered. In a rehearsal, a colleague asked her to state the question first, select the evidence relevant to it, and explain the practical conclusion. She kept the full tables in an appendix for questions. The revised structure did not hide the detail; it separated the main line of reasoning from material that listeners might need to inspect later.",
            sq("What changed in the presentation structure?", "The question and reasoning guided the selected evidence.", "All survey evidence was removed.", "The appendix replaced the entire talk.", "Question first, ilgili kanıt ve sonuç, ana akıl yürütme hattını kurar."),
            sq("Why were full tables retained?", "For later inspection and questions", "To make the figures impossible to check", "To replace the stated question", "Appendix, ayrıntının soru aşamasında incelenmesine açık kalır."),
            "The talk shows key findings; the appendix contains the complete tables.",
            sq("Does selecting key findings necessarily hide all detail?", "No, complete detail remains available.", "Yes, the tables have been destroyed.", "The talk contains no findings.", "Appendix complete tables içeriyorsa seçicilik ayrıntıyı bütünüyle gizlemez.")),
        s(21, "A dashboard compared customer satisfaction across teams but showed only average scores. One team had a similar average to another while receiving both very positive and very negative responses. The analyst added the distribution and the number of responses. This made the variation visible and prevented a simple ranking from concealing different experiences. She also warned that a team with very few responses should not be compared with the same confidence as one with many.",
            sq("What did the averages conceal?", "Differences in how responses were distributed", "The existence of any customers", "Proof that every team performed identically", "Aynı ortalama, çok olumlu ve çok olumsuz yanıtların dağılımını gizleyebilir."),
            sq("Why does the number of responses matter?", "Small response counts limit confidence in comparisons.", "It always guarantees a higher score.", "It makes every average irrelevant.", "Few responses, karşılaştırma güvenini sınırlayan örneklem bilgisidir."),
            "Two teams average four points, but one has two responses and the other has two hundred.",
            sq("What should the comparison acknowledge?", "Different amounts of supporting data", "Identical evidence strength", "A guaranteed difference in quality", "Ortalama eşit olsa da dayandığı veri miktarı farklıdır.")),
        s(22, "An employee noticed that an internal presentation used a colleague's analysis without acknowledging her contribution. He raised the issue privately with the presenter rather than accusing him in front of the audience. The presenter said the omission had been accidental and corrected the slides before the external meeting. The employee could not know the original intention with certainty, but he could identify the missing credit and request a concrete correction.",
            sq("What could the employee establish directly?", "Credit was missing from the presentation.", "The presenter's intention was certainly malicious.", "The analysis had never been produced.", "Missing credit gözlenebilir; original intention kesin bilinmiyor."),
            sq("What was the requested practical response?", "Acknowledging the contribution", "Cancelling every external meeting", "Inventing another author", "Corrected slides, katkının belirtilmesiyle somut düzeltmedir."),
            "The attribution is missing; I cannot judge the intention, but it needs to be corrected.",
            sq("What does the statement separate?", "An observable omission from an uncertain motive", "All responsibility from the need for action", "Authorship from every correction", "Eksiklik kesin olarak saptanırken niyet konusunda ihtiyat korunur.")),
        s(23, "A class discussed a proposal that would reduce emissions in one region but increase transport distances for some suppliers. Supporters emphasised the regional benefit; critics focused on effects outside the boundary used in the report. The tutor asked students to state the boundary before comparing the claims. The two positions were not necessarily inconsistent: a change could improve one measure while worsening another. A fair discussion needed to specify which effects were included and whose costs were counted.",
            sq("Why was the report's boundary important?", "It determined which effects were counted.", "It proved every external effect was zero.", "It made comparison unnecessary.", "Boundary, hesaba katılan bölge ve etkileri belirler."),
            sq("Can the two positions both describe real effects?", "Yes, they may refer to different measures or boundaries.", "No, any benefit rules out every cost.", "No, regional measures never exist.", "Bir ölçütte iyileşme, başka ölçütte kötüleşmeyle birlikte olabilir."),
            "Local traffic falls, but deliveries travel farther outside the town.",
            sq("Which summary is balanced?", "There is a local benefit and a possible external cost.", "All transport everywhere decreases.", "No local change occurs.", "Local ve outside sınırları farklı etkileri birlikte gösterir.")),
        s(24, "A student wrote that a study proved a policy was successful. The source actually said the findings were consistent with improvement under the conditions examined. In revision, she replaced the stronger verb and specified those conditions. She also explained why the study was relevant to her argument rather than inserting a quotation without comment. The paragraph became less absolute, but more defensible because its claim matched the evidence and its connection to the argument was explicit.",
            sq("What made the original wording too strong?", "It claimed proof where the source reported limited consistency.", "It mentioned the study at all.", "It avoided every conclusion.", "Proved ile consistent with farklı kesinlik düzeyleri taşır."),
            sq("What did the revised paragraph add?", "Conditions and an explanation of relevance", "A claim covering every possible situation", "An unrelated quotation with no comment", "Conditions ve relevant to her argument iddiayı sınırlar ve bağlar."),
            "The source says the result may support the policy in this setting, not that it proves universal success.",
            sq("Which wording stays closest to the source?", "The result offers limited support in this setting.", "The policy is proven to succeed everywhere.", "The result contains no relevant information.", "May ve this setting sınırlı desteği belirtir."))
    )
}
